                <pb facs="1048" n="928" sameAs="frus:frus1922v01/pg928"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">861.77/2798: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Minister in China</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                        >Schurman</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of
                    State</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Peking</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1922-10-31T16:00:00+08:00"><hi rendition="#italic">October 31,
                                1922—4 p.m.</hi></date><lb/>[Received 7:32 p.m.]</dateline></opener>
                <p>432. Your 253, October 27, 4 p.m. Note delivered to Foreign Office today.
                    British, French and Japanese Legations also delivered notes of similar purport.
                    Italian Legation will join in representations as soon as instructions are
                    received from Rome.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Schurman</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
